Step 1: Start with Basics (VERY IMPORTANT)

These are the foundation for almost everything:

Percentage ⭐ (Start FIRST)
Ratio and Proportion
Decimal Fraction
Simplification

👉 Why first?
Because topics like Profit & Loss, Interest, Average all depend on these.

📊 Step 2: Apply Basics to Real Problems

Once you're comfortable:

Average
Profit and Loss
Simple Interest
Compound Interest

👉 These are scoring and commonly asked in interviews.

🧠 Step 3: Logic + Thinking-Based Topics
Problems on Ages
Probability
Permutation and Combination

👉 These need understanding + practice (not just formulas).

🔢 Step 4: Slightly Advanced / Less Frequent
Square Root and Cube Root
True Discount
Chain Rule

👉 Usually fewer questions but still important.

